ed/**` alongside the hand-written pages, so a\nregenerated reference invalidates the build and the sidebar picks the new headings up with no\nextra wiring."],[219,"The generator lives in `docs/generate_shell_docs.py`. It is intentionally kept simple (stdlib only) but is being improved for even nicer output formatting."],[43,"The generator now produces:"],[2856,"The golden rule and why heavy workloads are dangerous around power events"],[1076,"The host `hermes-lab` stack is a **persistent lab operator*&#x2A;. Coder and Kasm workspaces use a separate &#x2A;*`workspace-dev`** profile for coding assistance:"],[598,"The image starts Hermes `workspace-dev` in the background on session launch. Desktop shortcuts open the dashboard (`:9119`) and Hermes CLI."],[1883,"The lab portal **Agent Chat** panel shows prerequisites, deploy/stop controls, and launch links."],[2972,"The lab uses **production-grade Traefik v3** (official Helm chart) as the unified HTTPS entry point, with **Authelia** for user management and forward-auth SSO. K3s bundled Traefik stays disabled; the standalone Helm install supports CRD middleware chains, TLS, and metrics."],[68,"The MkDocs site published two aliases with **mike**; Fumadocs has no mike equivalent, so the\nsame URLs are produced by building the static export twice with different `basePath` values:"],[4572,"The model"],[4533,"The model is TP=1 (many Nemotron nano/super, Qwen3.6 dual, MedGemma)"],[1029,"The multi-arch **devcontainer** can install the Hermes **CLI** (`hermes`) for\nlocal agent-assisted coding — see dev-environment.md.\nThat is separate from this page’s **host Docker gateway** on DGX Spark nodes.\nNever commit API keys or `hermes/data/.env` from either path."],[2163,"The multi-arch `.devcontainer/` image (linux/amd64 + arm64) includes bazelisk, buildifier, shfmt, ruff, mypy, ansible, kubectl, helm, kubeconform, shellcheck, bats, yamllint, Node.js 22, Python 3.11, Playwright, and a pinned Grok Build CLI. Versions and checksums are